CHAPTER VII

IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN

Rights of Women

Article 51

Women have the right to obtain education and training in work, positions, and professions in accordance with the requirements that have been determined.

Article 52

(1) Women have the right to choose, be elected, be appointed, in work, positions, and professions in accordance with the requirements and laws and regulations.

(2) Women have the right to obtain special protection in the implementation of their work or profession against matters that may threaten their safety and or health in relation to the reproductive function of Women.

(3) Special rights inherent to Women due to their reproductive function are guaranteed and protected by law.

IMPLEMENTATION OF VICTIM RECOVERY

Article 60

(1) The implementation of recovery activities for women and child victims includes:

a) Health services;

Health services are provided by health workers at health facilities owned by the government, regional government, and the community, including the private sector by providing medical treatment and health recovery services for victims.

b) Victim assistance;

Victim assistance is provided by health workers, social workers, volunteer assistants, and/or spiritual counselors by providing counseling, therapy, spiritual guidance and advocacy for the strengthening and recovery of victims.

c) Counseling;

Counseling is provided by social workers, volunteer assistants, by listening empathetically and exploring problems for the psychological strengthening of victims.

d) Spiritual guidance;

Spiritual guidance is provided by spiritual counselors by providing explanations regarding their rights and obligations, as well as strengthening faith and piety in accordance with the religion and beliefs they adhere to.

e) Resocialization.

Resocialization of victims is carried out by social agencies and social institutions so that victims can resume their social functions in society.

Article 45

In addition to the rights of Persons with Disabilities as referred to in paragraph (1), children with disabilities have the right to:

a. receive special Protection from Discrimination, neglect, harassment, exploitation, as well as sexual violence and crimes;

b. receive family care and upbringing or substitute family to grow and develop optimally;

c. have their interests protected in decision-making;

d. treatment of children in a humane manner in accordance with the dignity and rights of the child;

e. Fulfillment of special needs;

f. equal treatment with other children to achieve social integration and individual development; and

g. receive social assistance.

